ent-3729863364","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114780","id":3729863364,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eUTLE","user":{"login":"Jsjosie","id":122704241,"node_id":"U_kgDOB1BRcQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/122704241?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jsjosie","html_url":"https://github.com/Jsjosie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jsjosie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jsjosie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jsjosie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jsjosie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jsjosie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jsjosie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jsjosie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jsjosie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Jsjosie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T17:16:52Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T17:16:52Z","body":"Ok I see.Thanks for the clarification.\r\nI saw it from users perspective only so I didn't think of this.\r\nI agree that improving the documentation might be the better approach here.\r\nThanks for taking the time to give feedback for my assignment as well.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3729863364/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3730160180","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114780#issuecomment-3730160180","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114780","id":3730160180,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7eVbo0","user":{"login":"dalexeev","id":47700418,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3NzAwNDE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47700418?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev","html_url":"https://github.com/dalexeev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dalexeev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-09T18:47:45Z","updated_at":"2026-01-09T18:47:45Z","body":"> Expression is _not_ GDScript, it's a separate system that just happens to look like GDScript\r\n\r\nWhile I agree that this is true and important (`Expression` will never fully support all of GDScript's features), I'm not sure that it's justified in this particular case. The `&\"StringName\"` syntax is already used not only in GDScript, but also in text serialization (`var_to_str()`), as well as in other places that use it (`*.tscn` and `*.tres` files, documentation). Given this, I would say that users' assumptions about `Expression`'s support for `&\"StringName\"` syntax are also valid.\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\nprint(var_to_str(&\"test\")) # &\"test\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n```tscn\r\n[node name=\"Node\" type=\"Node\"]\r\nscript = ExtResource(\"1_0l1yd\")\r\ntest = &\"test\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n<img width=\"590\" height=\"68\" alt=\"\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fa4e3262-5b1c-4b6c-861a-833c8a98fcdd\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repo